What is Terraform?
Its a tool used to make infrastructure automation.
its a free and not open source
its platform independent
it comes on the year of 2014
who:Mitchel Hashimoto
Owned:Hashicorp-->recently IBM is maintaining.
terraform is written on the go language.
We can call terraform as IAC tool.
it is cloud Agonistic(it can used to work with any cloud and even it can manage things from onprem also)

How it works?
terraform used code to automate the infra.
we use HCL: Hashicorp Configuration Language.

IAC: Infrastructure as a code

code--->execute-->Infra

Advantage:-
1.Reusable
2.Time Saving
3.Automation
4.Avoiding mistakes
5.Dry run (Do not Repeat Yourself)

Cloud Alternatives:-
CFT=AWS
ARM=AZURE
GDE=GOOGLE

TERRAFORM=ALL CLOUDS

Terraform Vs Ansible
Terraform will create server
and these servers will be configure by ansible.

Installing Terraform on Linux:
Step-1:Installing Terraform

sudo yum install -y yum-utils shadow-utils
sudo yum-config-manager --add-repo https://rpm.releases.hashicorp.com/AmazonLinux/hashicorp.repo
sudo yum -y install terraform

terraform --version

Note:Terraform is 3rd Party Tool, so we need to give permission to terraform to work with AWS

Step:2 Giving IAM Role
aws configure 

MAIN ITEMS IN FILE:
blocks
lables (name, type of resource)
arguments

Configuration files:
it will have resource configuration.
here we write inputs for our resource
based on that input terraform will create the real world resources.
extension is ".tf"

first create a terraform folder/directory
mkdir terraform
Get into the folder
cd terraform
create main.tf

terraform code:-

provider "aws" {
    region="eu-north-1"
}

resource "aws_instance" "one" {
    ami="ami-03eb6185d756497f8"
    instance_type="t3.micro"
}

I-->init
P-->plan
